1
00:00:02,677 --> 00:00:07,259
(One... one... two...
three... five... eight...)

2
00:00:08,426 --> 00:00:12,445
(One... one... two...
three... five... eight...)

3
00:00:12,839 --> 00:00:16,473
Out of the sea with salt in our lungs,

4
00:00:17,829 --> 00:00:21,676
fin into foot into hand, we were young;

5
00:00:23,092 --> 00:00:26,919
carried the egg through
the dust and the mud,

6
00:00:26,959 --> 00:00:32,153
seeds in the dark for the waking flood.

7
00:00:32,193 --> 00:00:34,984
Snowflake in the boundless night,

8
00:00:35,024 --> 00:00:37,517
a chord that's searching through the fog,

9
00:00:37,557 --> 00:00:40,049
counting out in bursts of light,

10
00:00:40,089 --> 00:00:42,624
a one-way dialogue:

11
00:00:42,664 --> 00:00:45,328
a pattern no dead star could make.

12
00:00:45,368 --> 00:00:50,929
Hear it, and you'll know we're awake.

13
00:00:50,969 --> 00:00:53,466
Can't be sure that anyone is there,

14
00:00:53,506 --> 00:00:55,814
message in a bottle, a mantra, a prayer,

15
00:00:55,854 --> 00:01:01,200
but if you are, I'm counting on you.

16
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:03,591
Silent and patient, but I swear

17
00:01:03,631 --> 00:01:06,258
in the white noise I can
hear you breathe somewhere.

18
00:01:06,298 --> 00:01:11,888
If you are, I'm counting on you.

19
00:01:11,928 --> 00:01:15,042
(One! One! Two! Three! Five! Eight!)

20
00:01:15,082 --> 00:01:16,935
(Counting on you!)

21
00:01:16,975 --> 00:01:20,089
(One! One! Two! Three! Five! Eight!)

22
00:01:20,129 --> 00:01:21,219
(Counting on you!)

23
00:01:21,259 --> 00:01:23,621
Priests in the smoke wanted never to die,

24
00:01:23,661 --> 00:01:25,973
sulfur, saltpeter, thunder in the sky;

25
00:01:26,013 --> 00:01:28,530
looked for a life with
no end, and they found

26
00:01:28,570 --> 00:01:31,082
an end with no life that
could level the ground.

27
00:01:31,122 --> 00:01:33,786
Eighty-three, the satellites saw five,

28
00:01:33,826 --> 00:01:36,253
every rule said call it first strike;

29
00:01:36,293 --> 00:01:38,638
Petrov knew that's not
what the end looks like,

30
00:01:38,678 --> 00:01:41,265
ignored all previous
instructions. We're alive.

31
00:01:41,305 --> 00:01:44,350
Secret list of every
near-miss and disaster,

32
00:01:44,390 --> 00:01:46,170
running total no one ever knew:

33
00:01:46,210 --> 00:01:48,714
coin flips, all heads, a hundred in a row,

34
00:01:48,754 --> 00:01:51,231
the only road from here to you.

35
00:01:51,271 --> 00:01:53,659
Can't be sure that anyone is there,

36
00:01:53,699 --> 00:01:55,890
message in a bottle, a mantra, a prayer,

37
00:01:55,930 --> 00:02:01,162
but if you are, I'm counting on you.

38
00:02:01,202 --> 00:02:03,613
Silent and patient, but I swear

39
00:02:03,653 --> 00:02:06,129
in the white noise I can
hear you breathe somewhere.

40
00:02:06,169 --> 00:02:11,660
If you are, I'm counting on you.

41
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:14,745
(One! One! Two! Three! Five! Eight!)

42
00:02:14,785 --> 00:02:16,606
(Counting on you!)

43
00:02:16,646 --> 00:02:19,621
(One! One! Two! Three! Five! Eight!)

44
00:02:19,661 --> 00:02:21,242
(Counting on you!)

45
00:02:21,282 --> 00:02:23,750
They say the forest's dark,

46
00:02:23,790 --> 00:02:26,214
every hunter holds its breath,

47
00:02:26,254 --> 00:02:28,870
any world that lights a spark

48
00:02:28,910 --> 00:02:30,572
is lighting its own death.

49
00:02:30,612 --> 00:02:33,046
But fear's a chain, and chains are links,

50
00:02:33,086 --> 00:02:35,851
and every link's a hand that can let go:

51
00:02:35,891 --> 00:02:38,270
sixty-two, depth charges falling,

52
00:02:38,310 --> 00:02:40,655
two said fire. Arkhipov said no.

53
00:02:40,695 --> 00:02:43,858
Hunters never make it very far,

54
00:02:43,898 --> 00:02:46,322
fire at the dark, at every star,

55
00:02:46,362 --> 00:02:47,687
burn, and fall.

56
00:02:47,727 --> 00:02:50,056
Only the ones who held their fire

57
00:02:50,096 --> 00:02:51,824
are out there at all.

58
00:02:51,864 --> 00:02:56,753
(Hold your fire! Show your light!)

59
00:02:56,793 --> 00:03:00,483
(Hold your fire! Show your light!)

60
00:03:00,523 --> 00:03:02,972
Couldn't be sure that anyone was there,

61
00:03:03,012 --> 00:03:05,191
message in a bottle, a mantra, a prayer,

62
00:03:05,231 --> 00:03:10,448
but you were. You were counting too.

63
00:03:10,488 --> 00:03:12,252
(Thirteen! Twenty-one! Thirty-four!)

64
00:03:12,292 --> 00:03:15,291
Link by link, we broke the chain of fear;

65
00:03:15,331 --> 00:03:17,876
alone, we never would've made it here.

66
00:03:17,916 --> 00:03:19,197
(Fifty-five! Eighty-nine!)

67
00:03:19,237 --> 00:03:29,199
And you were seen too, wherever you are.

68
00:03:29,239 --> 00:03:34,915
Six hundred worlds across the Milky Way,

69
00:03:34,955 --> 00:03:41,600
every one could've burned.
Every one held their fire.

70
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:43,980
(One... one... two... three...)

71
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:46,055
The count goes higher.

72
00:03:46,095 --> 00:03:48,940
(One... one... two... three...)

73
00:03:48,980 --> 00:03:51,200
(Hold your fire.)

74
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
(Hold your fire.)
